# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in as needed.
# Any variable consumed by the browser must be prefixed with `VITE_`.

# ── Slow Lane (VLM) endpoint ──────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL. The Slow Lane picks an endpoint at build time in this order:
#
#   1. VITE_OLLAMA_URL (this var)  → any Ollama-compatible server, e.g. a
#      Cloudflare Tunnel exposing your own Ollama. Use `npm run tunnel`
#      to spin one up automatically.
#   2. `vite dev` (VITE_OLLAMA_URL unset, DEV mode)
#      → /api/ollama, proxied to 127.0.0.1:11434 by vite.config.ts.
#   3. Production build (VITE_OLLAMA_URL unset, PROD mode)
#      → /api/vlm, a Cloudflare Pages Function backed by Workers AI
#        (see functions/api/vlm.ts + wrangler.toml). This is the default
#        for `npm run deploy` and needs no extra configuration.
#
# Set this var only if you prefer to route the hosted site at your own
# Ollama (e.g. for Qwen3-VL specifically). Ollama must allow requests
# from the deployed origin:
#   OLLAMA_ORIGINS="https://voiceeye.pages.dev,https://*.voiceeye.pages.dev"
#
# VITE_OLLAMA_URL=https://ollama.example.com
